e/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c96bc838-492f-59b2-a5c3-daafd5bda8cf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c96bc838-492f-59b2-a5c3-daafd5bda8cf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c96bc838-492f-59b2-a5c3-daafd5bda8cf" :answer/id #uuid "c96bc838-492f-59b2-a5c3-daafd5bda8cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{60}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cf6946f6-4d9a-5dfa-9d8c-e7453ac9a280" :question/id #uuid "cf6946f6-4d9a-5dfa-9d8c-e7453ac9a280" :question/math-academy-id "q-196452" :question/problem "Roy, Kate, and Connor divided $\\frac{1}{3}$ of a watermelon equally among themselves. What part of a watermelon did each of the $3$ friends get?\n\nExpressed as a fraction, each of the friends got \n{{field-1}} of a watermelon." :question/worked-solution "To determine the part of the watermelon each friend got, we must divide the amount of watermelon by the number of friends.\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷3\n$$\n\nTo divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷3=\\frac{1}{3\\times 3}=\\frac{1}{9}\n$$\n\nTherefore, each of the $3$ friends got $\\frac{1}{9}$ of a watermelon." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b70428d8-80ed-5498-a096-4e874867f837"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b70428d8-80ed-5498-a096-4e874867f837" :answer-field/id #uuid "b70428d8-80ed-5498-a096-4e874867f837" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7196f476-ec0c-5138-920f-259220ec5944" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7196f476-ec0c-5138-920f-259220ec5944"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7196f476-ec0c-5138-920f-259220ec5944" :answer/id #uuid "7196f476-ec0c-5138-920f-259220ec5944" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0862a0c0-458a-56cf-9e21-ed5b94c7b818" :question/id #uuid "0862a0c0-458a-56cf-9e21-ed5b94c7b818" :question/math-academy-id "q-91869" :question/problem "Peter prepares $\\frac{1}{3}$ of a liter of coffee to distribute, in equal quantities, to his $5$ guests. How much coffee will each guest receive?" :question/worked-solution "To find out how much coffee each guest will receive, we have to divide the amount of coffee by the number of guests:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷5\n$$\n\nTo divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷5=\\frac{1}{3\\times 5}=\\frac{1}{15}\n$$\n\nTherefore, each guest will receive $\\frac{1}{15}$ liters of coffee." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c3f482b7-543c-5540-9c36-d9cf314f546b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c3f482b7-543c-5540-9c36-d9cf314f546b" :answer-field/id #uuid "c3f482b7-543c-5540-9c36-d9cf314f546b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-79f44679-b080-5eb9-b312-82b61b0215c2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5028e209-6cc3-5588-a8a9-97984bf1448d" "answer-048b0bbd-918a-58a6-9205-bfee63652b96" "answer-79f44679-b080-5eb9-b312-82b61b0215c2" "answer-39731579-f3cb-574a-8bc5-f7a7d3d64050" "answer-3f8ccd2d-67db-5176-8a5b-0c438cd7684a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5028e209-6cc3-5588-a8a9-97984bf1448d" :answer/id #uuid "5028e209-6cc3-5588-a8a9-97984bf1448d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{10}$ liters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-048b0bbd-918a-58a6-9205-bfee63652b96" :answer/id #uuid "048b0bbd-918a-58a6-9205-bfee63652b96" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{12}$ liters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-79f44679-b080-5eb9-b312-82b61b0215c2" :answer/id #uuid "79f44679-b080-5eb9-b312-82b61b0215c2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{15}$ liters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39731579-f3cb-574a-8bc5-f7a7d3d64050" :answer/id #uuid "39731579-f3cb-574a-8bc5-f7a7d3d64050" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{8}$ liters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f8ccd2d-67db-5176-8a5b-0c438cd7684a" :answer/id #uuid "3f8ccd2d-67db-5176-8a5b-0c438cd7684a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{3}{5}$ liters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fa95cd0e-dc98-58e2-b9c5-ac52a083197b" :question/id #uuid "fa95cd0e-dc98-58e2-b9c5-ac52a083197b" :question/math-academy-id "q-197135" :question/problem "Sam has $\\frac{1}{3}$ cubic meters of wooden boards to make $2$ dog houses. If he uses the same amount of boards for each dog house, how many cubic meters does Sam use for each dog house?\n\nExpressed as a fraction, Sam uses\n{{field-1}} cubic meters of boards for each dog house." :question/worked-solution "To determine the amount of boards used for each dog house, we divide the total amount of boards by the number of dog houses.\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷2\n$$\n\nTo divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷2=\\frac{1}{3\\times 2}=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Sam spent $\\frac{1}{6}$ cubic meters of boards for each dog house." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bbb8a4f9-7f3c-55c2-ac3a-3b4d2bb27fd0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bbb8a4f9-7f3c-55c2-ac3a-3b4d2bb27fd0" :answer-field/id #uuid "bbb8a4f9-7f3c-55c2-ac3a-3b4d2bb27fd0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-71e1770e-c062-5537-bc64-69414203755f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-71e1770e-c062-5537-bc64-69414203755f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71e1770e-c062-5537-bc64-69414203755f" :answer/id #uuid "71e1770e-c062-5537-bc64-69414203755f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3ecabb9b-a95d-572c-bb9e-7f166638bf38" :question/id #uuid "3ecabb9b-a95d-572c-bb9e-7f166638bf38" :question/math-academy-id "q-196453" :question/problem "Zoe distributed $\\frac{1}{2}$ kilograms of sausage equally between $4$ cats. How much sausage did each cat receive?\n\nExpressed as a fraction, each cat received\n{{field-1}}  kilograms of sausage." :question/worked-solution "To determine the amount of sausage per cat, we must divide the amount of sausage by the number of cats.\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}÷4\n$$\n\nTo divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}÷4=\\frac{1}{2\\times 4}=\\frac{1}{8}\n$$\n\nTherefore, each cat received $\\frac{1}{8}$  kilograms of sausage." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9da29b90-1776-59ee-ad83-0e3c57929e56"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9da29b90-1776-59ee-ad83-0e3c57929e56" :answer-field/id #uuid "9da29b90-1776-59ee-ad83-0e3c57929e56" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d5d430b1-54f0-522d-849a-87bd80279e9a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d5d430b1-54f0-522d-849a-87bd80279e9a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5d430b1-54f0-522d-849a-87bd80279e9a" :answer/id #uuid "d5d430b1-54f0-522d-849a-87bd80279e9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-38810655-0448-5128-9773-0f9ac772e869" :question/id #uuid "38810655-0448-5128-9773-0f9ac772e869" :question/math-academy-id "q-196454" :question/problem "A farmer divided his field into $3$ smaller lots of equal area. What is the area of each lot if the total area of the field is $\\frac{1}{2}$ acres?\n\nExpressed as a fraction, the area of each lot is\n{{field-1}} acres." :question/worked-solution "To determine the area of each lot, we divide the total field area by the number of lots.\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}÷3\n$$\n\nTo divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}÷3=\\frac{1}{2\\times 3}=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of each lot is $\\frac{1}{6}$ acres." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1dd78603-dcaf-519c-8371-d7573129f2bf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1dd78603-dcaf-519c-8371-d7573129f2bf" :answer-field/id #uuid "1dd78603-dcaf-519c-8371-d7573129f2bf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-08a8925b-df15-5136-9a6e-fca7a8915100" :answer-field/choices ["answer-08a8925b-df15-5136-9a6e-fca7a8915100"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08a8925b-df15-5136-9a6e-fca7a8915100" :answer/id #uuid "08a8925b-df15-5136-9a6e-fca7a8915100" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186075045 :tutorial/content "To divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by the whole number.\n\nFor example, to calculate $\\dfrac{1}{5} \\div {\\color{blue}2},$ we multiply the fraction's denominator by ${\\color{blue}2}\\!:$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{5} \\div {\\color{blue}2}  = \\dfrac{1}{5 \\times {\\color{blue}2}} = \\dfrac{1}{10}\n$$\n\nNotice that we get the same answer using a fraction model, and the process is similar.\n\n![](images/3f/3f1f0dddd115c0d820de4d79624bd87492e215a6c2de43071fda73a4a0684d77.png)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073950 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
